<title>UK: Lloyd's details results of fifth capacity auction.</title>
<headline>Lloyd's details results of fifth capacity auction.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-09-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Lloyd's of London on Friday issued the results of its fifth auction of capacity for the insurance market's 1997 underwriting year.</p>
<p>In this auction, held between 9-12 September, a total of 494 million stg of market capacity was auctioned, realising a total value of 9.5 million stg.</p>
<p>Subscription orders (offers to buy) entered during the fifth auction totalled 832 million stg, while tenders (offers to sell) totalled 641 million stg.  </p>
<p>Cumulatively, the five auctions held this year have resulted in 1.23 billion stg of capacity (representing 12 percent of 1996 underwriting capacity) being auctioned, realising 26 million stg in respect of 121 Lloyd's syndicates.</p>
